#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - OHOS musl keeps the gets symbol, only the
# declaration is gated behind C11 (reverse genus of E093)
# Source package: blimps/3.9 path-update audit (B-1 rewritten on OHOS facts)
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-musl-gets-decl-gated-symbol-retained
trigger_tool:           clang|musl|gets
phase:                  build|test_package
error_signature:        implicit declaration of function 'gets'|call to undeclared library function 'gets'|implicit-function-declaration.*gets

severity:               2
category:               platform-libc|deprecated-api|declarations|hardening
match_keywords:         musl, OHOS, gets, fgets, C11, __STDC_VERSION__, gnu17, implicit function declaration, command-line macro, bounded read, ld-musl, legacy C, K&R
title:                  OHOS musl keeps the gets symbol and gates only its declaration behind C11: legacy calls just warn, link and run, so a command-line macro is bounded-read hardening rather than a required fix

root_cause:             musl stdio.h gates the gets() declaration with
                        `#if __STDC_VERSION__ < 201112L` (C11 removed the
                        function). Under the default gnu17 mode the
                        declaration is hidden, so legacy gets() call sites
                        only emit -Wimplicit-function-declaration warnings;
                        the linker then resolves them against the real T
                        gets symbol exported by ld-musl (address distinct
                        from fgets/getline), and both build and run
                        succeed. This is the reverse genus of E093 ("musl
                        does not implement X -> build failure"): here the
                        symbol is retained and only the declaration is
                        hidden.
affected_scope:         Porting diagnosis for any legacy C project that
                        calls gets() on OHOS (ubiquitous in pre-C11
                        codebases); blimps 3.9 has 129 call sites.
verification_cmd:       /data/service/hnp/bin/llvm-nm -D /lib/ld-musl-aarch64.so.1 | grep -wE "gets|fgets|getline" && printf '#include <stdio.h>\nint main(void){char b[8];gets(b);puts(b);return 0;}' | /data/service/hnp/bin/clang -xc - -o "$TMPDIR/getsprobe" && echo ok | "$TMPDIR/getsprobe"

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           command-line-macro-bounded-fgets
rec_description:        Redirect every gets(s) call site with one
                        preprocessor define on the make command line,
                        -D'gets(s)=fgets(s,8192,stdin)' (covers all 129
                        blimps call sites with zero source changes).
                        Honest tradeoff: unbounded read -> 8KB bounded
                        read is a semantic change; it is hardening /
                        technical-debt retirement, not a repair of a
                        build failure, and must be declared in
                        notes/README.
rec_command:            make DEFINES="-D'gets(s)=fgets(s,8192,stdin)'" ... (protomat: append the same define to CFLAGS)
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      keep-as-is-accept-warnings
fallback_description:   Keep upstream semantics and accept the
                        implicit-declaration warnings; the build is
                        unaffected because the symbol is retained.
                        Fully legal, zero-risk option.
fallback_command:       ""
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual

fallback2_priority:     3
fallback2_approach:     per-call-site-fgets-patch
fallback2_description:  Rewrite each call site to fgets (Debian-style
                        gets.patch + more_gets.patch, ~53KB for blimps);
                        upstreamable but heavy to maintain, and the
                        bounded-length choice still needs the same
                        semantic declaration as the macro route.
fallback2_command:      ""
fallback2_auto_fix:     false
fallback2_impl:         patch

forbid_1_pattern:       musl (has no|lacks|removed|dropped) gets|gets.*(undefined symbol|undefined reference).*musl|musl.*gets.*build fail
forbid_1_reason:        Factually wrong root cause: OHOS musl retains a
                        working gets symbol (nm-verified T gets in
                        ld-musl); only the declaration is C11-gated.
                        Writing "musl has no gets -> build failure" into
                        notes/Issue/drafts misstates the mechanism and
                        pollutes the correct E093 genus.
forbid_1_consequence:   Knowledge-graph genus confusion; future porting
                        diagnosis starts from a false mechanism and
                        mis-classes working builds as failures.

forbid_2_pattern:       (define|implement|provide).{0,24}\bgets\s*\(
forbid_2_reason:        Hand-writing a gets() symbol implementation
                        revives an API removed from C11 precisely for its
                        unbounded-write hazard.
forbid_2_consequence:   Reintroduces the stack/heap overflow hazard that
                        the standard removed.

forbid_3_pattern:       shared header .*#define gets|#define gets\(.*in (a |the )?public header
forbid_3_reason:        A global #define gets in a shared/public header
                        leaks into every translation unit that includes
                        it, silently rewriting unrelated code and any
                        future use of the (gated) real declaration.
forbid_3_consequence:   Cross-package compile breakage far beyond the
                        affected library.

principles:             P-CFLAGS-001, P-PATCH-003
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:             [E093]
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:

